flowchart TB
    accTitle: Architecture — three places with clear responsibilities
    accDescr: The browser owns the screen and current conversation. The app server owns requests, AI tools, and SQL checks. PostgreSQL stores the queried data, while a separate AI provider receives model requests. Startup checks and saved schema information support these core responsibilities.
    %% Companion guide: docs/architecture.md

    BROWSER["Browser: Screen and current conversation"]:::view
    APP["App server: Requests, AI tools, and SQL checks"]:::work
    DB[("PostgreSQL: Stores the data you query")]:::data
    AI["AI provider: Generates SQL and explanations"]:::work
    CACHE["Saved table and column list: Avoid repeated database discovery"]:::data
    START["Default server startup: Check the database before serving"]:::note

    BROWSER <-->|Questions and responses| APP
    APP <-->|Checked queries and rows| DB
    APP <-->|Model requests and replies| AI
    APP -.-> CACHE
    START -.-> APP

